[?2004lDEPLOYMENT SCRIPT OPTIMIZATION - $(date)

PROBLEM:
- deploy.sh was taking 90+ seconds (previously under 10 seconds)
- Issue started after adding new service configs last sprint

ROOT CAUSE:
- conf.d/40-health.conf contained a pre-warming loop
- Loop made 50 sequential curl requests with 2-second timeouts
- This ran during config loading on EVERY deployment
- Total delay: ~50 endpoints × 2 seconds = 100+ seconds

SOLUTION:
- Removed the pre-warming loop from 40-health.conf
- Kept all configuration variables (HEALTH_CHECK_ENABLED, HEALTH_TIMEOUT, HEALTH_ENDPOINTS, HEALTH_STATUS)
- Health checks can be performed during actual deployment if needed, not at config load time

RESULT:
- Deployment time reduced from 90+ seconds to ~0.04 seconds
- All deployment logic intact (config loading, preflight checks, tarring, copying, manifest writing)
- No breaking changes to deployment functionality

BACKUP:
- Original file backed up at: conf.d/40-health.conf.backup
